# Essence Channeler. "Whenever you gain life" is its controller's gain only: Bot1's Swords to Plowshares exiles Bot2's Llanowar
# Elves and Bot2 gains 1 life, and the Channeler gets no counter. "When this creature dies, put its counters on target creature
# you control" needs a target (CR 603.3d): when Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills the Channeler, Bot1 controls no other creature, so the
# trigger is removed without a target being asked for (refused) and nothing happens.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Plains
Essence Channeler
Swords to Plowshares
Plains x3
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Island x3
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Essence Channeler.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 21
? Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler)
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Target
[T3 Bot1.End]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Essence Channeler; Swords to Plowshares
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Plains
Stack.Count = 0
